            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "A standard deck of cards is shuffled and the top and bottom cards are drawn, without replacement. Find the probability that the two cards satisfy the following.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p24-q12-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Have the same colour.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{25}{51}$",
          "worked": "Whatever the colour of the top card, 25 of the remaining 51 cards have that colour.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(\\text{same colour})&=\\frac{25}{51}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p24-q12-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Have the same suit.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{4}{17}$",
          "worked": "Whatever the suit of the top card, 12 of the remaining 51 cards have that suit.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(\\text{same suit})&=\\frac{12}{51}\\\\P(\\text{same suit})&=\\frac{4}{17}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 46
      },
      {
        "id": "p24-q12-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Have the same rank (A, 2–10, J, Q or K).",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{1}{17}$",
          "worked": "Whatever the rank of the top card, three of the remaining 51 cards have that rank.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(\\text{same rank})&=\\frac{3}{51}\\\\P(\\text{same rank})&=\\frac{1}{17}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 46
      },
      {
        "id": "p24-q12-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "Are face cards (J, Q, K).",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{11}{221}$",
          "worked": "There are 12 face cards. If the top card is a face card, 11 face cards remain among the other 51 cards.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(\\text{both face cards})&=\\frac{12}{52}\\times\\frac{11}{51}\\\\P(\\text{both face cards})&=\\frac{11}{221}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 46
      }
    ]
